{"annotationDigest":"sha256:146ba517ce6ffcdf7c9e5a83746fb02e98f99606cc3fcb24eeaead7639aa82c8","annotationId":"rann-d989603ea2f2bcacc0b448edce13bf1f","author":{"agent":"claude-code","kind":"ai","model":"claude-opus-5.5"},"createdAt":"2026-10-02T06:56:20Z","disclaimer":"AI-generated review opinion derived from the evidence package. It is not a verdict, does not change readiness, and must be confirmed by a human reviewer.","disclosureCheck":{"blocking":6,"contradictions":[],"disclosures":8,"nextDecision":"human_judgement","readiness":"not_assessed"},"findings":[{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:stripJsonc","SW-REQ-260922-E4J2"],"scenario":"a user menu JSONC loaded via Menu.qml FileView whose second line is a // comment indented with U+00A0 (or U+3000, VT, FF, U+2028, U+FEFF): at base parseMenuJsonc returns every entry; at head it returns [] and logs 'MenuModel: failed to parse menu JSONC'"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"This is a regression the PR introduces, not an acceptable compatibility change. The removed regex `^\\s*\\/\\/[^\\n]*(\\n|$)` (m flag) deleted ANY JS whitespace in front of a whole-line comment; JS `\\s` includes VT, FF, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000-U+200A, U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000 and U+FEFF. The new scanner (MenuModel.js:25) drops only the `//...` text and copies the indent; JSON.parse accepts only space/tab/LF/CR, so the parse fails, the catch returns [] and the new console.warn fires. I ran base vs head MenuModel.js in node on `{\\n<ch>// note\\n \"a\":..., \"b\":...}`: base 2 rows, head 0 rows for NBSP, U+3000, VT, FF, U+2028, BOM, U+1680, U+202F; tab/space 2 rows at both. The green tripwire test 'KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE tripwire' in test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs (menu-node suite, joined in the JUnit report) passes on this tree for all 21 such characters against an ASCII-indented control; I ran it against the base MenuModel.js and it fails there (the base keeps both rows). Compat finding cf-39627352fe66ab9c is unapproved. It breaks SW-REQ-260922-E4J2 on this input partition. Quickshell's FileView drops a LEADING BOM (per the KI and the menu-test.sh input-domain comment, Quickshell 0.3.1; not re-checked here), so only a BOM at file start is masked; the same characters on any later comment line trigger it. Suggested fix (KI remediation, as #13968 b2dae8db does): copy any JS whitespace outside a string as one ASCII space, keep LF. Settle with the suggested test.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":25},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1047},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"review.compat","kind":"check"}],"severity":"high","title":"REGRESSION (cf-39627352fe66ab9c, KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE): a whole-line comment indented with non-JSON JS whitespace now empties the whole menu file","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Comment-lines-only Unicode indent partition (E4J2 input_domain)\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"Function-level trace on stripJsonc (MenuModel.js:8-35) and parseMenuJsonc. The scanner widens comment stripping from whole-line comments to any `//` outside a JSON string, honouring `\\\"` escapes. E4J2's own input_domain witness for comment indentation (menu-test.sh:270-286) was turned on this mirror from a nominal witness into the regression's tripwire (finding 0), so the E4J2 input_domain cell is observed_pass on its remaining witnesses, not on that partition.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":8},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-test.sh","kind":"file","