sed; six compatibility changes await a reviewer."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":0,"rationale":"Pins the old regex behaviour: for each JS \\s character outside JSON whitespace, a file whose (non-first) comment line is indented with it must parse like the ASCII-indented control. Fails at head today; restore the baseline witness at menu-test.sh:278 once fixed, and add the mode to the bdiff data generator.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1047},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-test.sh","kind":"file","line":278},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","kind":"requirement"}],"title":"Comment-lines-only Unicode indent partition (E4J2 input_domain)"},{"forClaim":16,"rationale":"Settles parity of the scanner and console.warn between node and the shell's engine.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1044},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","kind":"requirement"}],"title":"Live QV4 witness: inline-comment and malformed user extension in the menu-live suite"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** omacom/omarchy#6525 (head 913e112d) replaces stripJsonc's line-anchored comment regex with a string-aware scanner: a `//` comment after content on a line is dropped, `//` inside strings (URLs, after `\\\"`) is kept; the trailing-comma pass is unchanged. parseMenuJsonc now logs a console.warn on a parse failure. Mirror commit c0f4600e is the upstream change; cdb0f3df..9a44345b are our proof work (witnesses, a bound KI tripwire, KI records, trace re-review).\n\n**Is the fix verified?** For its purpose, yes: 16/16 changed decisions covered, 57/57 tests passed and current; the #13493 corpus inputs go from 0 to 3 rows (bd-05efa2ff, bd-41c905c2, classified intended). KI-MENU-JSONC-INLINE-COMMENT is fixed. Cells: 21 observed_pass, 27 not_linked.\n\n**Questions for a human.** The PR introduces a REGRESSION (cf-39627352fe66ab9c, KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE, new_defect): a whole-line comment indented 